      en: "The Nature Trail in Karthala Forest is a 3.5 km loop that winds through montane cloud forest at elevations between 600 and 900 m. It features 12 interpretive signs explaining the ecology and endemic species, such as the Comoro olive pigeon and the Karthala scops owl. The trail takes about 2 hours to complete. It was established in 2015 by the Comoros National Park service. The forest acts as a vital watershed for the island. The trail is maintained by local guides who also offer birdwatching tours.",
